```
Jump buffering & attack timers in physics.

Keyboard listeners:
- keydown: set keys; if Space and !repeat → jumpPressed=true (buffered), prevent default; F/KeyJ/Enter → attackPressed; Q/KeyE/ShiftRight? → dash; KeyM mute.
- keyup: Space → jumpHeld=false? variable jump cut handled in physics via `jumpCutQueued` when released while rising.

We'll set `input.jumpQueued = true` on keydown, and `input.jumpCut = true` on keyup (consumed in physics if vy>0).

Also mouse drag orbit and wheel zoom; canvas click for attack if not dragged.

Touch:
- stick pointerdown/move/up as before, with joy normalized (-1..1), knob style.
- buttons jump/dash/attack pointerdown set queues.
- canvas pointer drag orbit for touch outside controls: Track pointerdown on canvas: if pointerType touch or mouse → start drag; pointermove → camYawOffset, pitch; pointerup → if small movement and mouse → attack? For mouse maybe click = attack. Implement click attack only for mouse (not touch) to avoid accidental.

But the start screen overlay covers canvas, so canvas events only after started. Add `pointer-events` on canvas default.

Physics step function:

```js
const FIXED = 1/120;
const P = {
  radius: .42, walk: 5.7, sprint: 9.6, dashSpeed: 17.5,
  gravity: 30, fallGravity: 39, jumpV: 9.6, doubleJumpV: 8.4,
  maxFall: 34, accelGround: 52, accelAir: 24, friction: 18
};
const playerState = {
  vel: new THREE.Vector3(), vy: 0, grounded: true, coyote: 0, jumpBuffer: 0,
  jumpsLeft: 2, stamina: 100, exhausted: false, staminaDelay: 0,
  dashTimer: 0, dashCooldown: 0, dashDir: new THREE.Vector3(0,0,-1),
  attackTimer: 0, attackCooldown: 0, attackHit: false, combo: 0, comboTimer: 0,
  invuln: 0, hurtTimer: 0, squash: 0, walkPhase: 0, runBlend: 0, airBlend: 0, dashBlend: 0,
  idleTime: 0, lastGroundY: 0, speed: 0, wasGrounded: true, facing: 0, shake: 0, hitstop: 0
};
```

Attack: `triggerAttack()` sets timer if cooldown<=0. Attack total .4. Hits applied at timer crossing? Use `attackHit` false; in physics when attackTimer < .24 and !attackHit → check hits. Combo increments if last attack within .7s.

Damage to enemies function.

`hurtPlayer(amount, fromX, fromZ)`.

`addShards(n)`.

`updateCamera(dt)`.

`animatePlayer(dt)`.

Enemy step:

```js
function stepEnemies(dt){
  for each e alive:
    e.timer -= dt;
    const dx=player.x-e.g.position.x, dz=..., d=hypot;
    if (state.started && d<15) {
      // eye face player
      if (e.grounded && e.timer<=0) { hop toward player; e.timer=0.65+rnd()*0.5; }
    }
    // gravity
    e.vy -= 26*dt;
    e.g.position.y += e.vy*dt;
    // horizontal move
    e.g.position.x += e.vel.x*dt; e.g.position.z += e.vel.z*dt;
    // friction
    e.vel.x *= exp(-2.2*dt);
    ...
    const gy = heightAt(...);
    if (e.g.position.y <= gy) { landing squash if falling fast; y=gy; vy=0; grounded=true; }
    else grounded=false;
    // face player when close
    // collision with player → hurt
    // terrain boundary (keep r<66)
  }
}
```
Hopping: on ground when timer<=0 and distance<14: vy=4.6; vel = dir * (elder?2.2:2.9); timer=.6+rnd*.5. Also if player very close, short hop attack. Keep simple.

Enemy squash visual in animateWorld: scale y = 1 + clamp(vy*0.05) etc. Since group scale also size, use e.g. base scale s * (1 - squash*0.35) etc. Actually we set g.scale = s initially; animate with s*(x,y,z). Use e.squash for landing pulse.

Face player: rotate g smoothly to atan2(-dx,-dz)? Model face is at -Z. yaw = atan2(-dx,-dz) points face toward player? Face at -Z, so yes yaw = atan2(-dx,-dz).

Hurt player if d < 0.75+0.42 and player near ground height; apply.

Attack hitting enemies:
```js
const fwd = new THREE.Vector3(0,0,-1).applyQuaternion(player.quaternion) // player rotation y
for each e: dx,dz; d<2.9; dot(fwd, dir)>0.1; if (vertical diff<1.8)
  damage; knockback e.vel += dir*6; e.vy=2.4; e.hurtFlash=.18; e.hp -= dmg;
  spark burst, shake, hitstop .06, audio.hit
  if hp<=0: killEnemy
```
Kill: e.alive=false; scene.remove(e.g); spark burst; addShards(1); toast.

Player collision with enemy also push player slightly.

Camera-relative input inside step:
```js
let fwdInput = (keys.KeyW||keys.ArrowUp?1:0) - (keys.KeyS||keys.ArrowDown?1:0) - joy.y;
let sideInput = (keys.KeyD||keys.ArrowRight?1:0) - (keys.KeyA||keys.ArrowLeft?1:0) + joy.x;
const wishX = (-Math.sin(camYaw))*fwdInput + Math.cos(camYaw)*sideInput;
const wishZ = (-Math.cos(camYaw))*fwdInput + (-Math.sin(camYaw))*sideInput;
```
Check: camForward = (-sin(camYaw), -cos(camYaw)); camRight = (cos(camYaw), -sin(camYaw)). At camYaw=0: forward (0,-1) i.e. -Z ✓; right (1,0) ✓.

Normalize >1.

Sprint check: (keys.ShiftLeft||keys.ShiftRight||joy magnitude>0.92) && stamina>1 && wishLen>.2 && !exhausted.

Stamina logic before setting max speed:
```js
const wantSprint = shift && wishLen>.2 && !ps.exhausted && stamina>1;
let speed = wantSprint? P.sprint : P.walk;
if (wading) speed *= .55; if (slope) speed *= .85;
ps.stamina = clamp(ps.stamina + (wantSprint? -21: 17)*dt,0,100)
if (ps.stamina<=0) ps.exhausted=true;
if (ps.exhausted && ps.stamina>24) ps.exhausted=false;
```
No regen delay needed; simple.

Dash:
```js
if (input.dashQueued && ps.dashCooldown<=0 && ps.stamina>=16) { ... input.dashQueued=false; }
```
Set vel directly; timer .22; stamina -= 16; dashCooldown .8; invuln .3? player invuln for dash → yes 0.25 (avoid damage).

During dash:
```js
if (ps.dashTimer>0) {
  ps.dashTimer -= dt;
  const k = 0.55 + 0.45*(ps.dashTimer/0.22);
  ps.vel.x = ps.dashDir.x*P.dashSpeed*k; ...
  ps.vy = Math.max(ps.vy, -1); // float
  if (rnd()<... ) spawn streak
} else normal accel.
```
Note dash should cancel attack.

Jump:
```js
ps.jumpBuffer = Math.max(0, ps.jumpBuffer-dt);
if (input.jumpQueued){ ps.jumpBuffer=.14; input.jumpQueued=false; }
if (ps.jumpBuffer>0 && ps.grounded) { jump }
else if (ps.jumpBuffer>0 && ps.jumpsLeft>0) { double jump }
```
jumpsLeft init 2; on ground reset to 2 in landing; on jump from ground → jumpsLeft=1? Then double jump consumes → 0. If jumpsLeft=2 while grounded, jumping sets jumpsLeft=1. Air jump when jumpsLeft>0 (even if walked off edge) → consume. Good.

After jump: input.jumpCut should not apply. If released while rising, apply cut once.

Physics order:

```js
function stepPlayer(dt){
  // timers
  ...
  // input wish
  ...
  // grounded? determine using heightAt at current x,z and player.y
  const gy = heightAt(x,z);
  const onGround = ps.grounded;
  // jump
  ...
  // dash
  ...
  // horizontal accel
  ...
  // slope handling
  const n = normalAt(x,z);
  if (ps.grounded && n.y < 0.72) { slide }
  // integrate
  let nx = x + vel.x*dt; let nz = z + vel.z*dt;
  // collisions + boundary
  ...
  player.position.x = nx; player.position.z = nz;
  // vertical
  if (!ps.grounded) { vy -= grav; y += vy*dt; }
  const gy2 = heightAt(nx,nz);
  if (player.position.y <= gy2 + 0.001) { land } else if (ps.grounded && player.position.y > gy2 + 0.3) { grounded=false }
  if (ps.grounded) { player.position.y = gy2; ps.vy=0; }
  ...
}
```
Careful with jump pose: set grounded false and y += .03; then the ground check in same step: y = gy+.03 > gy, so stays airborne; then vertical integration happens? Put vertical integration before ground check with `if(!grounded)`. Jump sets grounded false then integration applies gravity immediately (fine) → y increases slightly. Ground check y<=gy false. Good.

When grounded, we want y=gy continuously and jump sets vy. Sequence:

```
// jump may set grounded=false, vy=JUMP
integrate x,z (with slope logic using grounded before? fine)
if (!grounded) { vy -= grav*dt; y += vy*dt; }
// resolve collision
// ground check
if (grounded) { y = gy; vy=0; }
else if (y <= gy) { land; }
```

But when grounded on a slope and moving, y set to new gy ✓.

If jump just happened (grounded=false, vy>0), y += vy*dt and check y<=gy → false. Good.

Landing detection: `if (!grounded && y <= gy)`: impact = -vy before zero; set y=gy; vy=0; grounded=true; jumpsLeft=2; coyote=.11; squash... if impact > 8 heavy landing → extra dust/shake.

Walking off a ledge: since terrain is smooth, gy follows; no cliffs. But when landing from a jump, okay.

Coyote: if grounded → coyote=.1, jumpsLeft=2; else decrement.

Slope slide: n = normalAt; if grounded && n.y < 0.70 → add along downhill: downhill = (n.x, n.z) normalized * (0.70-n.y)*45*dt; plus if very steep disable input? Fine.

Steep uphill block: compute dot(wish, uphill) where uphill = (n.x,n.z) (points downhill? gradient: normal x = hL-hR of height gradient negative? For terrain, normal = (-dh/dx, 1, -dh/dz) so n.x points toward decreasing height → downhill. Hmm check normalAt: (hL-hR, 2e, hD-hU) = (-2e*dh/dx, 2e, -2e*dh/dz) → n.x = -dh/dx, which points downhill (opposite gradient). So (n.x,n.z) is downhill. Uphill = -(n.x,n.z). If moving uphill on steep slope, reduce accel. Simpler: speed *= clamp(1 - (1-n.y)*0.6, 0.55, 1) and add slight downhill drift when n.y<.8. Good.

Boundary: 
```js
const r=Math.hypot(nx,nz);
if (r>64){ const k=(r-64)*0.5; nx-=nx/r*k; nz-=nz/r*k; // also damp outward velocity
}
if (heightAt(nx,nz) < -1.1) { push toward center }
```
But terrain at r=64 might already be water (islandMask from 40 to 71 → at 64 mask ~0.25 → h ~ -2.4). Hmm, island edge at r≈71 water. Let's allow up to r=62; land height at r=62: m = 1-smoothstep(40,71,62) = 1-smoothstep=1-0.92? compute: t=(62-40)/31=.71; smooth=3t²-2t³=.87 → m=.13 → h=-4.6+1.18+noise ≈ -3.4 → underwater. So walkable land ends ~r=52? m at 52: t=.387, smooth=.355 → m=.645 → h=-4.6+5.87=1.27. At 58: t=.58, smooth=.62 → m=.38 → h=-1.14. So shoreline around r=55-60. Good: island radius ~60 with beach at 50-58.

Given shard positions up to 48 and enemies 46, all on land. Boundary clamp at r=58 with water push when h<-0.6. Player can wade a bit. Let's implement:
- soft wall at r=57 pushing inward.
- if h < -0.8 at new pos → strongly push inward (and slower).

Splash particles when wading speed>2.

Collision grid resolution: keys around cell.

After collisions, also collide enemies? no.

Combat and attack timers:
```js
ps.attackCooldown = max(0, -dt)
ps.attackTimer = max(0, -dt)
if (input.attackQueued) { input.attackQueued=false; if (cooldown<=0) startAttack() }
```
startAttack: attackTimer = .42; attackCooldown=.34; attackHit=false; combo = (comboTimer>0? combo+1:0)%3; comboTimer=.8; audio.attack(); camera kick.

Apply hit when attackTimer <= .26 && !attackHit && attackTimer>0. In step: if (attackTimer>0) { if(!attackHit && attackTimer<=.28){ attackHit=true; doHit(combo===2?2:1); } }.

Attack animation uses attackTimer ratio: `p = 1 - attackTimer/.42`.

Damage player: invuln; health--; shake .5; flash; knockback vel += dir*6; vy=3.5; grounded=false; audio hurt; if health<=0 → after .6s respawn? Simplify immediate: health=5; health reset; teleport to spawn; shards keep; toast. Could be jarring; add fade using CSS flash. Keep.

Invuln flashing avatar visible toggling: during invuln, avatar.visible = sin(t*40)>-0.3. Fine, but ensure visible at end.

Respawn if fall in water? Height never below -5, water y=0, so player can wade; if h<-2 (deep), push back.

Now `updateVisuals(dt)`:
- animate avatar; shadow light follow; crystals animate + collect; shrine animate; pollen; particles; enemies visuals; clouds; sun sprite; water time; map.
- Also HUD.

`updateCamera(dt)`.

