Map draw:
```js
function buildMapBg(){...}
function drawMap(){ ctx.clearRect; save; clip circle; drawImage(bg,0,0,150,150); icons; player; restore }
```
Mapping: worldToMap x → 75 + x*(70/72)? Island radius ~60 land, water beyond. Use scale 68/72 ≈ .94. Use size 150: center 75. World r=72 → 68px. Fine.

Bg draw per pixel using heightAt with world range ±80 and 150 px → color. Sample step 1px.

Colors: h<-1 deep teal; <-0.1 shallow; <0.8 sand; else greens with shading by gradient. Water outside r>?? all deep beyond island. Add coastline stroke? not necessary.

Map icons: shards small cyan diamonds; enemies red dots (alive, not shown if >? show all), shrine gold star, player arrow.

HUD: hearts creation once:
