```
activate: state.won=true; beam opacity target 1; quest text; audio.win; sparks burst; set timeout 1400ms show win screen; winStats text `3 SUNSHARDS · 2:14 · ...`; win time = state.time.

Shrine detection each frame if started && !won && distance < 5.6 → tryShrine with cooldown; else reset flag when >7.

Now the loop:

```js
let last=performance.now(), acc=0;
function frame(now){
  requestAnimationFrame(frame);
  const raw = Math.min(0.05, (now-last)/1000); last=now;
  state.time += raw;
  const speedScale = state.hitstop>0 ? 0.18 : 1;
  state.hitstop = Math.max(0, state.hitstop - raw);
  if (state.started) {
    acc += raw * speedScale;
    let n=0;
    while(acc>=FIXED && n<5){ stepPlayer(FIXED, raw); stepEnemies(FIXED); acc-=FIXED; n++; }
    if(n===5) acc=0;
    updateInteractions(raw); // shrine, pickups
  }
  animateAvatar(raw);
  updateEnemiesVisual(raw);
  updateWorld(raw);
  updateCamera(raw);
  drawMap();
  updateHud();
  renderer.render(scene,camera);
  hideLoading();
}
```
Enemies step only if started; pre-start they idle.

Hitstop affects player and enemies both via scaled accumulation (good).

But animateAvatar uses real time (still animates during hitstop) fine.

`updateInteractions`: shards magnet/collect, shrine proximity, pollen? etc.

